; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Delaware enters the 2028 presidential race as an open contest, with the incumbent president term-limited and neither party yet fielding a named nominee. The state's partisan lean favors Democrats by about eight points, giving the Democratic ticket a structural head start. No public polls of the race, expert ratings, candidate fundraising totals, or prediction-market pricing are available, so the picture rests on the state's underlying partisanship.\n\nThe Democratic nominee, whoever emerges from a primary that remains fluid, starts with a clear but not insurmountable edge. Uncertainty is elevated because the national environment and the identity of both nominees remain unsettled, leaving room for the race to move in either direction as the campaign develops.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8204, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7838, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7798, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7761, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7732, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.8108, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.771, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7706, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7752, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7784, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7742, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7744, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.7814, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.7654, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.7761, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.7809, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.803, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.7904, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.8172, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.7605, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-13", "p_dem